{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And they shall wash in water.</b> The reason for Scripture's mentioning his washing — our Sages, of blessed memory, said (Torat Kohanim) — is to equate for her the law of her washing according to all the conditions alluded to in the law of his washing. And if you would say: if this is what the verse intended, it was not necessary, for we would have derived it from His saying ״וְאִשָּׁה״ — the additional vav adding to the first matter, to equate the law of both of them and to apply what is stated of the upper one to the lower one, as they expounded in Torat Kohanim in the portion of Vayikra for all those laws written with a vav at the beginning. But according to what our Sages, of blessed memory, expounded in Torat Kohanim — that ״וְאִשָּׁה״ with a vav comes to include a minor girl of three years and one day — accordingly, had it not said ״וְרָחֲצוּ,״ we would have expounded the vav for the laws of washing and would not have known the tumah of a minor girl of three years and one day." "And aside from their words, it would appear to say the following: according to what they said (in Torat Kohanim) regarding the verse ״אֲשֶׁר תֵּצֵא מִמֶּנּוּ שִׁכְבַת זֶרַע״ — until its tumah departs outside his flesh; but if it has not departed, even though he feels it, he grips the amah and consumes terumah — whereas the woman is impure even when she merely touches semen in her hidden place. Therefore it says ״וְרָחֲצוּ״ to say that Scripture equates the two of them only regarding washing, not regarding the law of tumah. And from this point we interpret His saying ״וְאִשָּׁה״ with a vav, for the woman too sometimes has an equal law to the man — she is not impure in her hidden place according to the Rabbans if he came upon her not in her natural way, and according to Rabbi Yehudah, the first intercourse of a bride (Torat Kohanim here, Yevamot 34:) — and they derived this for her from the word ״אוֹתָהּ.״ And from this point, had it not said ״וְרָחֲצוּ״ and I would have come to derive the laws of washing that apply to the man for the woman from the vav of ״וְאִשָּׁה,״ I would also have derived that the man imparts tumah even if the semen did not depart outside, and would have learned it from the woman. And I would have interpreted His saying ״תֵּצֵא״ to mean that its uprooting from its place is called ״going out,״ or on this path: ״תֵּצֵא״ is in the future tense — meaning, anything that is fit to go out, even if it has not gone out, is impure, just as we find by the woman. Therefore it says ״וְרָחֲצוּ״ to reveal to you that the vav of ״וְאִשָּׁה״ was not joined to apply what is stated of this one to that one. And if it had said ״וְרָחֲצוּ״ without the vav of ״וְאִשָּׁה,״ even though there is the word ״אוֹתָהּ״ from which they derive a restriction for the Master who says ״not in her natural way״ and for the Master who says ״the bride,״ even so we would not have expounded the word ״אוֹתָהּ״ in this manner, and we would have expounded ״אוֹתָהּ״ for another interpretation — since once it was revealed to us explicitly in the verse that he imparts tumah in the place of concealment, what difference is there — the bride, what difference, and so forth. And on the contrary, there would have been room to say ״אוֹתָהּ״ comes to include all her concealed places; but through His saying ״וְאִשָּׁה״ with a vav, Scripture equated them to other tumot of concealed places that do not impart tumah. And according to what they expounded in Torat Kohanim — ״וְאִשָּׁה״ to include a girl of three years and one day — they revealed their opinion that the word ״אוֹתָהּ״ is specifically designated to be expounded as a restriction and not as an inclusion, and therefore the vav of ״וְאִשָּׁה״ remains superfluous, and they expounded it for a girl of three years and one day."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "Resolved the ambiguous phrase בתוספת ו׳ as referring to the additional (additive) vav prefix on ״ואשה״, consistent with the Or HaChaim's argument throughout about the vav's exegetical function."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:30.252726076Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}